\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Single-modality conditioning has limitations in satisfying user intent. Image-only conditioning captures local appearance but omits unobserved regions; text-only conveys semantics but lacks visual fidelity. In contrast, joint text–image conditioning produces 3D assets that are both semantically aligned with the description and faithful to the reference appearance.}}{1}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
